        "changelog": "Two improvements found live while testing missing-metadata search. (1) The search loop stopped at the first attempt that returned ANY result, even a single wrong/below-threshold one - meaning a year-filtered search returning one irrelevant candidate meant the broader year-less attempt (the one actually likely to surface the real match) never ran at all. Every attempt (full title, archive-suffix-stripped title, each with and without year) is now tried and pooled together (deduplicated by name+year) before scoring. Each attempt's own query and result count is now logged too, and the \"no confident match\" line names the closest candidate found and its title-similarity score instead of just a bare count - makes it possible to tell whether a rejection was a title mismatch, a year mismatch, or genuinely nothing found. (2) The \"Current run\" live-progress tab now shows one row per library in scope for the run - not just the one currently being processed - with a library not reached yet showing \"n/a\" instead of being left out of the table entirely, so the full scope of the run is visible from the start.",
